{
; The retained block vocabulary belongs to in-memory render values and stable
 ; DOM ids. Namespace-page membership and ordering come from `render.walk`;
 ; nothing here declares or stores an agent-owned block set.
 :seon.render.block/name :keyword

 ; One of exactly two typed render outputs. A durable declaration stores the
 ; producer symbol; a renderer function returns the Hiccup arm. Explicit
 ; producer fields below narrow this union back to `:qualified-symbol`.
 :seon.render/html [:or :qualified-symbol :seon.render/hiccup]

 ; HICCUP IS A NAMED PREDICATE, and that is a limitation being paid for
 ; honestly rather than a preference. Hiccup is a tree, and a
 ; self-referential declaration currently overflows the stack in
 ; `seon.schema/bind-predicates` (issue
 ; a-self-referential-schema-overflows-the-stack). The supported idiom
 ; for a shape this registry cannot express is a registered core
 ; predicate with an honest generator, which is strictly better than
 ; `:any` here anyway: the grammar belongs to the serializer that
 ; enforces it, the predicate IS that grammar, and the generator's
 ; output domain is the serializer's input domain so every totality
 ; property generates against the real thing.
 :seon.render/hiccup [:fn {:gen/gen seon.render.hiccup/hiccup-generator} seon.render.hiccup/hiccup?]

 ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ; THE RENDERED PAGE
 ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

 ; The DOM element id, derived from the name by ONE function so the hole
 ; and the patch can never drift apart. `surface-` prefixed because the
 ; id shares a document with ids nobody here owns.
 :seon.render/surface-id [:string {:min 9}]

 ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ; DISTANCE — how many hops of the neighborhood one render reaches
 ; (owner ruling, 2026-07-28 post-midnight; seal revision to the request
 ; shapes below).
 ;
 ; NO NEW NOUN AND NO NEW KIND: distance is a REQUEST PARAMETER threaded
 ; to the renderers and to the one bounded expansion, exactly as caps and
 ; the trusted inputs already are. "The neighborhood view" is therefore
 ; the same page mechanism asked a different question, not a second one.
 ;
 ; THE CALL CONVENTION, and it is the whole design: distance is an
 ; argument TO the renderer, never a property OF it. The renderer is
 ; CALLED with the distance (present on the unit; IMPLIED 1 when absent,
 ; and never required — a projection that ignores it is correct).
 ; Reaching past one unit is the walk's compositional act: following a real
 ; database ref spends one hop and delegates the reached value to its owner.
 ; Distance 0 follows no connections.
 ;
 ; ACCRETION, strictly. Absent means exactly today's behaviour: the
 ; admission caps alone bound the walk. Distance never overrides those
 ; caps — the depth and node dials remain the absolute bound, and
 ; distance SELECTS WITHIN them.
 :seon.render/distance [:int {:min 0}]

 ; The shell's ordered hiccup fragment.
 :seon.render/page [:vector :seon.render/hiccup]
}
